{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ChannelSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ChannelSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.JetProlongation","lean:module:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.UniversalDifferentials"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.channelSeparates_iff_multi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.channelSeparates_iff_multi","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L183-L188","doc":"**Channel-separation activation theorem.**\n`channelSeparates n = true ↔ n ≥ 2` — proved directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.channelSeparates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.channelSeparates","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L175-L181","doc":"**Channel-separation activation predicate.**\nBoolean indicator of whether `n` strands witness\nmulti-generator structure. Defined as `decide (n ≥ 2)` so the\nqualitative fact that channel separation activates exactly for\n`n ≥ 2` is true by definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.kahler_differentials_no_sym_component","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.kahler_differentials_no_sym_component","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L132-L152","doc":"**Proposition**: the universal one-forms `Ω¹(A) = ker(μ : A ⊗ A → A)`\nhave no component along the unit section `A ⊗ 1`.\n\nPrecisely, `Ω¹(A)` and `A ⊗ 1` are complementary in `A ⊗ A`\n(`isCompl_Ω1_range_unitSection`), so they meet only in `0`.  This is the\nalgebraic content of \"`d(𝟏) = 0`\": the degree-0 piece of `A ⊗ A`, the\none `μ` maps isomorphically onto `A`, carries no differential forms.\n\nStated for any algebra `A` over a commutative ring `R`, commutative or\nnot, so it covers the Hecke realisation.  What is NOT formalised here is\nthe representation-theoretic reading in `H₃(q)`, where the summand `A ⊗ 1`\nis identified with the symmetric (trivial-representation) channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.level_to_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.level_to_degree","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L130-L130","doc":"Each jet level k corresponds to Hecke elements of word length ≤ k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.max_word_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.max_word_length","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L128-L128","doc":"The jet level ≤ maximal word length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.n","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L126-L126","doc":"The number of Hecke generators (= number of strands minus 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence","kind":"structure","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L102-L130","doc":"The **Hecke--jet correspondence**: the word-length filtration on\n`H_n(q)` corresponds to the jet level filtration on `J^k(A)`.\n\n| Jet level | Hecke degree | Elements |\n|-----------|-------------|----------|\n| `J^0(A)` | degree 0 | identity `𝟏` |\n| `J^1(A)` | degree 1 | single generators `σ_i` |\n| `J^k(A)` | degree ≤ k | words of length ≤ k in `σ_i` |\n\nThe kernel of `j^1 : J^1(A) → J^0(A) = A` is `Ω¹(A)`, which\ncorresponds to the degree-1 piece of the Hecke algebra (the\ngenerators modulo the identity).\n\nIn the graded decomposition:\n- `Ω¹(A)^{sym} = 0` (the symmetric component of the differential\n  forms vanishes, since `d(1) = 0` in the symmetric representation)\n- `Ω¹(A)^{std}` = the standard representation piece (degree 1)\n\nThis is why the 6×6 transfer matrix (which tracks ALL irreps) gives\nno new information per generator — but multi-generator products\n(corresponding to higher jet levels) DO separate the channels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.jet_compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.jet_compatible","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The jet object's Frobenius--Hopf data matches the grading's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.grading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.grading","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The base is a graded Frobenius--Hopf object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.jet","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The categorical jet data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.mk","kind":"ctor","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading","kind":"structure","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L79-L98","doc":"The **jet filtration** on the graded Frobenius--Hopf object.\n\nAt each jet level `k`, the grading `A = A^0 ⊕ A^{≥1}` induces\na grading on `J^k(A)`:\n- `J^k(A)^0 = J^k(A^0)` (jet prolongation of the symmetric component)\n- `J^k(A)^{≥1} = J^k(A^{≥1})` (jet prolongation of the high component)\n\nThe compatibility condition ensures that the jet evaluation\n`j^k : J^k(A) → J^{k-1}(A)` respects the grading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.adjoint_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.adjoint_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Adjoint vanishing at the base level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.adjointObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.adjointObj","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The adjoint object at the base level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.base","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The base graded Frobenius--Hopf object (level 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation","kind":"structure","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L58-L75","doc":"**Jet-graded channel separation data**: a graded Frobenius--Hopf\nobject at each jet level, with the grading compatible with\nthe jet prolongation structure.\n\nAt each level `k`:\n- `A_k = J^k(A)` has a graded decomposition `A_k = A_k^0 ⊕ A_k^{≥1}`\n- The jet evaluation `j^k : J^k(A) → J^{k-1}(A)` preserves the grading\n- The adjoint vanishing `Hom(𝟙, Ad(A_k)) = 0` holds at all levels ","signatureChunk":0}]}